{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1575995888,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2NDExOTcyOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3914#issuecomment-564119728"},"message":"My guess is, that we split the call to `git-commit`. By that we screw up the run record, which now is indistinguishable from running that script several times and - for whatever reason - affecting different files.\n\nWhat we prob. should do instead is `--amend`'ing when we split commit calls. What do you think, @kyleam ?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1575996965,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2NDExOTg1Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3914#issuecomment-564119856"},"message":"\u003e My assumption is that this is due to the number of files that I'm operating on. Curious on what you guys think.\n\nHmm I think your that's very likely it.  When running commands, `GitRepo._run_command_files_split` will chunk the command if it thinks the command might exceed the maximum line length.  I'm surprised that when `run` calls `save` without any files (as it should for the invocation that you described) that the underlying `git commit` call would be given any pathspecs though.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1575996965,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDMyMjYwMDU5Ng=="},"target":"aef7b80b5ae68d5c96f70ac90d24a7feeb5f1589c9d15a23f46a7c2af9322330","message":"\u003e My assumption is that this is due to the number of files that I'm operating on. Curious on what you guys think.\n\nHmm I think that's very likely it.  When running commands, `GitRepo._run_command_files_split` will chunk the command if it thinks the command might exceed the maximum line length.  I'm surprised that when `run` calls `save` without any files (as it should for the invocation that you described) that the underlying `git commit` call would be given any pathspecs though.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1575996042,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2NDEyMDk5MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3914#issuecomment-564120991"},"message":"\u003e  I'm surprised that when run calls save without any files (as it should for the invocation that you described) that the underlying git commit call would be given any pathspecs though.\n\nInteresting point indeed. I guess save without anything will inspect what to commit and make it explicit. Not sure, whether it actually should.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1575996549,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2NDEyNDg5NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3914#issuecomment-564124894"},"message":"\u003e What we prob. should do instead is `--amend`'ing when we split commit calls. What do you think, @kyleam ?\n\nYeah, I suppose so.  Special casing \"commit\" at the level of `_run_command_files_split` isn't pretty, but probably better than creating a chain of commits.\n\nIn the future, it looks like `git commit` will [gain][0] a `--pathspec-from-file` option that'd be useful in this situation, but we of course wouldn't be able to rely on that any time soon.\n\nI'd be interested to hear @yarikoptic's thoughts given he implemented the chunking, IIRC.\n\n[0]: https://lore.kernel.org/git/pull.445.git.1572895605.gitgitgadget@gmail.com/T/#u","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1575996848,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2NDEyNzI3Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3914#issuecomment-564127273"},"message":"\u003e \u003e What we prob. should do instead is `--amend`'ing when we split commit calls. What do you think, @kyleam ?\n\u003e \n\u003e Yeah, I suppose so. Special casing \"commit\" at the level of `_run_command_files_split` isn't pretty, but probably better than creating a chain of commits.\n\nThen again, given the \"clean index\" focus of the new `save`, shouldn't the case where we need to specify the files be very rare? Which leads back to figuring out why pathspecs were used in the first place for the situation described.  I'll have to look into that.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1575998104,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2NDEzNzAzMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3914#issuecomment-564137033"},"message":"- we should start using `--pathspec-from-file` whenever it comes about!\n- using `--amend` sounds also good and logical for this case (which is a workaround around POSIX limitations). I also wonder if in such cases (where we know that multiple --amends would happen due to largeish number of files), we could take advantage of `git -c core.splitIndex=true`? It would be interesting to time and see if any positive/negative effect\n\nrelated: https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3265 \"run: support \"covering\" multiple commits\"","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1575999291,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2NDE0MTczMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3914#issuecomment-564141733"},"message":"I said:\n\u003e  I'm surprised that when `run` calls `save` without any files (as it should for the invocation that you described) that the underlying `git commit` call would be given any pathspecs though.\n\nGlancing at the code, it doesn't look like a pathspec should be used in this case (no staged files).  Setting CMD_MAX_ARG ridiculously low\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/datalad/utils.py b/datalad/utils.py\nindex d40d00436..e58628caf 100644\n--- a/datalad/utils.py