nimal example that triggers the multi-commit behavior on your end?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"fcd7c5a83b52ec23265b2f0237a1af09934a0e5a"},"timestamp":1576150707,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2NDk3MTUzOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3914#issuecomment-564971539"},"message":"@kyleam I've re-created the directory/file structure of the dataset that I was working with (https://github.com/loj/test_dlrun), and included the shell script that I used with `datalad run`.\n\n\u003cdetails\u003e\u003csummary\u003ethe setup\u003c/summary\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\n\n```\ndatalad create test_dlrun\ncd test_dlrun\n\ncp ../dirs.txt ./\ncp ../files.txt ./\ndatalad save --to-git -m \"save list of files and directories\"\n\nxargs mkdir -p \u003cdirs.txt\nxargs touch \u003cfiles.txt \ndatalad save -m \"replicate dir/file structure\"\n\ncp ../convert.sh ./\nchmod +x convert.sh\ndatalad save --to-git -m \"save shell script\"\n\n```\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/details\u003e\n\nI was able to trigger the multiple commits via `datalad run -m \"trigger multiple runs\" \"./convert.sh\"`","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1576168322,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU2NTA4MjEwNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3914#issuecomment-565082105"},"message":"Thanks @loj.\n\nLooking at your script explains the mystery above (why `git commit` is being called with pathspecs).  The key thing is your script adds files to the index.  The stage changes result in the `datalad save` call (in particular `GitRepo.save_`) going down the code path that calls `git commit` with pathspecs, which in turn leads to the calls being split up to avoid failing due to exceeding the maximum command line length.  If you were to replace `git mv` with a plain `mv`, you shouldn't see multiple commits.  Here is a small test that demonstrates the issue:\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/datalad/core/local/tests/test_save.py b/datalad/core/local/tests/test_save.py\nindex 2bacaecc6..41640054f 100644\n--- a/datalad/core/local/tests/test_save.py\n+++ b/datalad/core/local/tests/test_save.py\n@@ -11,6 +11,8 @@\n import os\n import os.path as op\n \n+from unittest.mock import patch\n+\n from datalad.utils import (\n     on_windows,\n     assure_list,\n@@ -735,3 +737,15 @@ def test_save_obscure_name(path):\n     # Just check that we don't fail with a unicode error.\n     with swallow_outputs():\n         ds.save(path=fname, result_renderer=\"default\")\n+\n+\n+@with_tree(tree={\"foo\": \"foo\", \"bar\": \"bar\"})\n+def test_save_multicommit(path):\n+    ds = Dataset(path).create(force=True)\n+    ds.save()\n+    expected = ds.repo.get_hexsha()\n+    ds.repo.call_git([\"mv\"], files=[\"foo\", \"foo-moved\"])\n+    ds.repo.call_git([\"mv\"], files=[\"bar\", \"bar-moved\"])\n+    with patch('datalad.utils.CMD_MAX_ARG', 5):\n+        ds.save()\n+    eq_(ds.repo.get_hexsha(\"HEAD^\"), expected)\n```\n\nSo at this point we're at the state that @yarikoptic described in gh-3138:\n\n\u003e most likely would cause multiple commits instead of a single one for commit calls. But imho it would already be better than just crashing\n\nAs @bpoldrack suggested I think it'd be worth exploring how a patch to use `--amend` looks.\n\nI'll re-title this issue for clarity.","files":null},{"type":2,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1576168392,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE3OlJlbmFtZWRUaXRsZUV2ZW50Mjg3ODU4MTIwNw=="},"title":"Saving with (many) staged changes can produce multiple commits","was":"Saving with (many) staged changes can produce multiple commits"}]}